---
import MissionLayout from '../../layouts/MissionLayout.astro';
---

<MissionLayout
  slug="zippyzack"
  heading="ZippyZack.com"
  timeline="Launch planned for January 2027"
  status="Pre-launch / Live holding page"
  statusHref="https://www.zippyzack.com/"
  explorerGradient="linear-gradient(40deg, #005247 0%, #007f5f 100%)"
>
  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">1. The TL;DR <span class="case-section-sub">(Executive Summary)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Purpose</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Introduce ZippyZack with a playful, crochet-inspired identity ahead of its announced January 2027 launch. The public website gives the brand a home while the full experience is still to come.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Problem</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A pre-launch website needs to tell visitors what they have arrived at and when to return, without presenting an unfinished product as ready to use. Here, the immediate communication challenge is brand recognition and a clear launch expectation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Solution</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">A focused coming-soon page that pairs the message &ldquo;crocheting ZippyZack&rdquo; with a prominent launch date, an animated ball of yarn, and a warm, colourful visual identity.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">The Impact</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The holding page is publicly accessible and communicates a January 2027 launch. Traffic, conversion, customer adoption, and business outcomes are not publicly reported; this case study covers the pre-launch experience rather than a launched product.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">2. Strategy &amp; Discovery</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Communication Focus</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The page makes the act of making part of the message. &ldquo;Crocheting&rdquo; and the travelling yarn ball turn a waiting state into a craft-themed introduction, while the brand name and date remain the primary information.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Audience &amp; Scope</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The current experience serves visitors discovering ZippyZack before launch. The public page does not describe a product catalogue, shopping flow, team structure, or user research, so those details are outside the scope of this report.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Constraint</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Keep the promise specific without implying that the full offering is available. The visible page contains the brand and launch announcement, with no product navigation, checkout, or email sign-up.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">3. Execution <span class="case-section-sub">(The &ldquo;How&rdquo;)</span></h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Experience Structure</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The live page uses a single-screen composition rather than a multi-page product introduction: a compact brand mark at the top, a large central announcement, the launch date directly underneath, and decorative motion below. This keeps the available message easy to scan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Visual Identity &amp; Accessibility</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Forest green anchors a cream background, with mint, bright green, and lemon-yellow accents. Rounded Baloo 2 lettering gives the brand its playful voice, italic Newsreader distinguishes &ldquo;crocheting,&rdquo; and Nunito Sans carries the launch information. Layered waves, subtle grain, and a rolling yarn ball reinforce the handmade theme. Responsive styles adapt the composition to smaller screens, and a reduced-motion preference stops the yarn animation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Live Website</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value"><a class="case-link" href="https://www.zippyzack.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit ZippyZack.com ↗</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Visual Highlights</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Launch-page screenshots will be added here. The images below are placeholders, not ZippyZack product screens.</p>
      <!-- Gallery -->
      <div class="gallery-wrap">
        <div class="gallery-track-wrap">
          <div class="gallery-track" id="galleryTrack">
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/background-main.jpg" alt="Placeholder for a future ZippyZack screenshot" />
            <img class="gallery-img" src="/assets/projects/background-main.jpg" alt="Placeholder for a future ZippyZack screenshot" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="gallery-controls">
          <button class="gallery-btn" id="galleryPrev" aria-label="Previous">&#8592; Back</button>
          <span class="gallery-counter" id="galleryCounter">1 / 2</span>
          <button class="gallery-btn" id="galleryNext" aria-label="Next">Next &#8594;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
  
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section">
    <h2 class="case-section-title">4. Outcome &amp; Lessons</h2>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">KPIs</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">No public performance metrics are available. The verifiable delivery is the live holding page and its January 2027 announcement, not a measured improvement in engagement, sales, or retention.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Current Takeaway</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">The page illustrates how a small pre-launch surface can establish a recognisable tone through typography, colour, and a single craft metaphor. This is an observation of the published design, not a finding from user testing or post-launch usage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="case-field">
      <h3 class="case-field-label">Next Steps</h3>
      <p class="case-field-value">Document the full offering and its user journeys when they become public, add project screenshots, and update this report with confirmed delivery details and measured outcomes after launch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</MissionLayout>
